s, the system displays \'-\' instead of \'0\'.','<img style=\"width: 1262px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041538-zezlc.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 10:11:13','2026-04-13 06:08:42',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,15,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:08:42'),(16,1,1,'Society Onboarding → Manage Society Structure → Wing-->Newly added wing shoud be shown in first like last come first shown.','<img style=\"width: 1268px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041547-lriae.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 10:18:28','2026-04-13 06:08:04',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,16,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:08:04'),(17,1,1,'In Society Onboarding → Manage Society Structure → Floors: After creating a floor, it initially shows as inactive. However, when I navigate to Flats and then return to Floors, the status changes to active.','<img style=\"width: 1263px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041610-piun0.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 10:44:57','2026-04-13 06:07:39',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,17,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:07:39'),(18,1,1,'Society Onboarding → Manage Society Structure →In Flats: While trying to add flats, the added floors are not visible in the Add Flat form.','<img style=\"width: 1566px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041617-pdkps.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 10:48:41','2026-04-13 06:06:35',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,18,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:06:35'),(19,1,1,'Society Onboarding--> Manage society structure--> Search--> Rename Search to \"Search by Tower name\".','<img style=\"width: 1272px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041639-y4pwt.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-04-04 11:10:41','2026-04-13 06:05:26',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,19,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:05:26'),(20,1,1,'Society Onboarding--> Manage society structure--> Search--> Wing--> Rename Search to \"Search by Wing name\".','<img style=\"width: 1296px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041641-ygvod.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,5,'2026-04-04 11:12:11','2026-04-13 06:05:16',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,20,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:05:16'),(21,1,1,'Society Onboarding--> Manage society structure--> Search--> Floor--> Rename Search to \"Search by Floor name\".','<img style=\"width: 1282px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041642-8qclm.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-04-04 11:13:14','2026-04-13 06:05:07',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,21,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:05:07'),(22,1,1,'Society Onboarding--> Manage society structure--> Search--> Flat--> Rename Search to \"Search by Flat number\".','<img style=\"width: 1275px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041643-5mams.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-04-04 11:14:26','2026-04-13 06:04:30',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,22,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:04:30'),(23,2,1,'WebSocket Integration for Security & Resident Approval Flow (AVIGO App)','**Overview:**\r\nTo enhance real-time communication and reduce dependency on polling APIs, we will implement WebSocket-based event handling for the Security App and Resident App within the AVIGO ecosystem.\r\n\r\n**Objective:**\r\nEnable instant approval/rejection of visitor and service requests, improving response time, user experience, and operational efficiency.\r\n\r\n**Scope of Implementation:**\r\n\r\n1. **Real-Time Visitor Approval Flow**\r\n\r\n   * When a visitor entry is created by security, an event is pushed via WebSocket to the respective resident.\r\n   * Resident receives instant notification inside the app (without refresh).\r\n   * Resident can Approve / Reject directly.\r\n   * Response is sent back via WebSocket to security.\r\n\r\n2. **Security App Updates**\r\n\r\n   * Immediate status update (Approved / Rejected / Auto-Rejected after timeout).\r\n   * Reduced waiting time and manual follow-ups.\r\n\r\n3. **Auto-Reject Mechanism**\r\n\r\n   * If no action is taken within defined SLA (e.g., 1 hour), system auto-rejects request.\r\n   * Event triggered via backend scheduler and pushed to both apps.\r\n\r\n4. **Connection Handling**\r\n\r\n   * Token-based authentication for WebSocket connections.\r\n   * Reconnection strategy for unstable networks.\r\n   * User-specific channels (societyId / flatId based routing).\r\n\r\n5. **Scalability & Architecture**\r\n\r\n   * WebSocket server integrated with existing Node.js backend.\r\n   * Redis (Pub/Sub) used for horizontal scaling and event distribution.\r\n   * Supports multiple app instances and concurrent users.\r\n\r\n6. **Fallback Mechanism**\r\n\r\n   * If WebSocket is disconnected, fallback to push notifications or fire it any ways (FCM).\r\n   * Ensures no critical event is missed.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Benefits:**\r\n\r\n* Real-time experience for residents and security\r\n* Reduced API load (no polling)\r\n* Faster approvals → better security operations\r\n* Scalable and production-ready architecture\r\n\r\n**Dependencies:**\r\n\r\n* Redis (Pub/Sub)\r\n* Existing authentication system\r\n* Push notification service (fallback)\r\n\r\n**Notes:**\r\n\r\n* Implementation should not impact existing APIs.\r\n* Follow modular approach for easy future extension (e.g., chat, alerts).\r\n* Ensure backward compatibility with current app versions.\r\n\r\n','2026-04-06',NULL,5,12,3,NULL,1,5,'2026-04-04 11:16:55','2026-06-13 07:48:04','2026-04-04',0,NULL,NULL,23,1,2,0,'2026-06-13 07:48:04'),(24,1,1,'Society Onboarding--> Manage society structure--> Replace all over tower word into the Building word. ','<img style=\"width: 1261px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041647-woazr.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,5,'2026-04-04 11:18:35','2026-04-16 09:19:07',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,24,1,2,0,'2026-04-16 09:19:07'),(25,1,1,'In Society Onboarding → Buildings: Since flat numbers are not created in the Flat form, the structure is not visible here.','<img style=\"width: 1262px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041656-bnpel.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 11:29:19','2026-04-13 06:00:16',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,25,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 06:00:16'),(26,1,1,'In Society Onboarding → Manage Structure → Flats: When a flat is deactivated from the flat menu, the updated inactive status is only reflected after refreshing the page. The same issue occurs vice versa.','<img style=\"width: 1275px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041708-rtbll.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,10,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 11:40:26','2026-04-13 05:59:52',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,26,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:59:52'),(27,1,1,'In Resident → Add Resident → Flat Square Feet, entering a value greater than 10,000 shows an incorrect validation message. The field should restrict input above 10,000 instead of allowing it and displaying a wrong validation message.','<img style=\"width: 1284px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041727-jz8pv.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-04-04 12:02:39','2026-04-13 05:52:22',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,27,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:52:22'),(28,1,1,'In Society Onboarding → Residents, the Flat Square Feet field has a validation limit of 10,000, but it is currently accepting values greater than 10,000.','<img style=\"width: 1264px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041734-ziivq.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:14:25','2026-04-13 05:52:01',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,28,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:52:01'),(29,1,1,'In Residents → Edit, when editing the form, the previously selected dropdown values are not pre-selected.','<img style=\"width: 1284px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041747-0z2g8.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:20:14','2026-04-13 05:51:04',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,29,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:51:04'),(30,1,1,'Residents, all relevant fields such as Building, Wing, Floor, Flat Number, and Flat Type should be displayed.','<img style=\"width: 944px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041753-hufa3.png\"><br>\r\n<img style=\"width: 1262px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041753-t5p0r.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:24:32','2026-04-13 05:49:51',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,30,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:49:51'),(31,1,1,'Residents → After Edit, the updated flat details are not reflected in the listing.','<img style=\"width: 1264px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041755-eq6w1.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:26:34','2026-04-13 05:49:14',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,31,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:49:14'),(32,1,1,'Buildings--> Occupied, owner occupied, maintenance--> Need to be changed as mentioned by anoop.','<img style=\"width: 1282px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041800-4pepk.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:31:58','2026-04-16 09:08:19',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,32,1,2,0,'2026-04-16 09:08:19'),(33,1,1,'In Manage Society Structure → Flat Management, when a resident is added to a specific building, wing, floor, and flat, the Flat Type is not displayed for that occupied flat.','<img style=\"width: 1537px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041803-y7bsi.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:35:52','2026-04-13 05:46:27',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,33,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:46:27'),(34,1,1,'Resident--> message shown wrong, It should be \"Flat already Assigned to another user\". As well as if flats is already assigned that time no need to shown the assigned flat in the list for time management of admin.','<img style=\"width: 1286px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041814-apoa7.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,2,NULL,7,8,'2026-04-04 12:45:58','2026-04-16 09:24:43',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,34,1,2,0,'2026-04-16 09:24:43'),(35,2,1,'Resident User Management – Disassociate User from Flat (Feature)','We need to create a feature to **disassociate a user from a flat**.\r\n\r\n### 🔹 Purpose:\r\n\r\nTo handle scenarios like:\r\n\r\n* ownership transfer\r\n* resident changes\r\n\r\n### 🔹 Key Features:\r\n\r\n* Option to **remove user from a flat** without affecting the flat\r\n* Flat remains **active and billable**\r\n* User is no longer linked to that flat\r\n* Maintain **history/log** of association (who was linked earlier)\r\n* Allow **re-assignment of new user** to the same flat\r\n* Restrict action to **authorized roles (Admin/Super Admin)**\r\n\r\n### 🔹 System Behavior Changes:\r\n\r\n* After disassociation:\r\n\r\n  * User **should not be able to access flat-specific features**\r\n  * Login/session handling changed / destroyed\r\n  * If user has no flat → restrict or show limited access state\r\n\r\n* Ensure:\r\n\r\n  * No impact on other APIs\r\n  * Existing flows remain stable\r\n  * Proper validation added in middleware/services\r\n\r\n---','2026-04-11',NULL,5,12,3,NULL,1,3,'2026-04-04 12:48:55','2026-05-08 09:21:10','2026-04-04',0,NULL,NULL,35,1,2,0,'2026-05-08 09:21:10'),(36,1,1,'In Residents → Add, while adding a resident, it should be select multiple flats for a single resident. currently only one flat assigned.','<img style=\"width: 1267px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604041820-mhgtm.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,3,NULL,7,3,'2026-04-04 12:54:09','2026-04-13 05:32:49',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,36,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:32:49'),(37,1,1,'Avigo Admin--> Genaral MAster--> Flat Residence occupancy master--> Please add the all data in this master through the tables.','<img style=\"width: 1895px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604061044-od2ky.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,3,NULL,13,4,'2026-04-06 05:16:26','2026-04-13 05:30:23',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,37,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:30:23'),(38,1,1,'Avigo Admin--> Genaral Master--> Country Master--> After searching for unavailable data, \"No records found\" is displayed correctly, but after clearing the search field, the message still coming instead of showing all data.','<img style=\"width: 1903px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604061057-al9dc.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,2,NULL,13,3,'2026-04-06 05:29:01','2026-04-13 05:29:36',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,38,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:29:36'),(39,1,1,'Avigo Admin--> Genaral Master--> State Master--> Pagination is not working properly; unable to navigate to the next page.','<img style=\"width: 1833px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604061106-nidtk.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,12,2,NULL,13,3,'2026-04-06 05:37:11','2026-04-13 05:28:50',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,39,1,2,0,'2026-04-13 05:28:50'),(40,1,1,'Avigo Admin--> Genaral Master--> Amenities Master--> Duplicate entry adding here.','<img style=\"width: 1872px;\" src=\"clipboard-202604061122-prhd0.png\"><