e in the media list created the separete entry.','<img style=\"width: 1591px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607291830-nhayc.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-07-29 13:04:54','2026-08-03 07:33:01',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1934,1,2,0,'2026-08-03 07:33:01'),(1935,1,7,'except hoardings, not take the file as the fields are mismatch as we discussed.','<img style=\"width: 1546px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607291848-jm5wp.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-07-29 13:18:59','2026-08-03 07:30:02',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1935,1,2,0,'2026-08-03 07:30:02'),(1936,1,1,'federation - Federation guards should have access to all societies and their respective flats.  Need to shown the all residets data with their family members in the respective society.',' Resident Directory\r\nThe app\'s Resident Directory screen — browse every resident across the federation\'s assigned societies, each with their flats, family members, and tenants already expanded (no separate detail call needed). Filter by society or search. A fast type-ahead search endpoint is included below for attaching a resident while logging a visitor.\r\nResident directory (the screen)\r\nGET  /visitormanagement/federation-gate/residents/directory\r\nAuth role: fedration_security\r\nREQUEST\r\nField		Type / notes\r\nsocietyId	optional	uuid — filter to one society\r\nsearch	optional	string <=100 — name / mobile / flat\r\npage / limit	optional	int — default 20, max 100\r\n\r\nRESPONSE • DATA\r\n{\r\n  \"residents\": [ {\r\n    \"id\": \"...\", \"name\": \"...\", \"mobile\": \"...\", \"residentType\": \"...\",\r\n    \"societyId\": \"...\", \"societyName\": \"...\",\r\n    \"flats\": [ { \"flatNumber\": \"A-101\", \"building\": \"...\", \"wing\": \"...\", \"floor\": \"...\" } ],\r\n    \"familyMembers\": [ { \"name\": \"...\", \"mobile\": \"...\", \"relation\": \"...\" } ],\r\n    \"tenants\": [ { \"name\": \"...\", \"mobile\": \"...\" } ]\r\n  } ],\r\n  \"societies\": [ { \"societyId\": \"...\", \"societyName\": \"...\" } ],   // for the society filter\r\n  \"pagination\": { \"currentPage\": 1, \"totalPages\": 4, \"totalItems\": 80, \"pageSize\": 20 }\r\n}\r\nQuick search (type-ahead)\r\nGET  /visitormanagement/federation-gate/residents/search\r\nAuth role: fedration_security\r\nFast flat/resident lookup — used while logging a visitor to attach the flat & resident. Returns up to 20 matches.\r\nREQUEST\r\nField		Type / notes\r\nsearch	optional	string <=100 — flat / resident / mobile\r\nsocietyId	optional	uuid — scope to one society\r\n\r\nRESPONSE • DATA (ARRAY, MAX 20)\r\n[ {\r\n  \"flatId\": \"...\", \"flatNumber\": \"A-101\", \"societyId\": \"...\",\r\n  \"details\": \"Society - X, Building - Y, Wing - Z, Floor - 1\",\r\n  \"resident\": \"Resident: Priti Patil\",\r\n  \"residentName\": \"Priti Patil\", \"residentMobile\": \"...\", \"residentId\": \"...\"\r\n} ]\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,3,NULL,13,5,'2026-07-30 04:58:03','2026-09-02 11:02:11',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1936,1,2,0,'2026-09-02 11:02:11'),(1937,4,1,'federation - The Federation Security should be responsible for managing all Federation Staff. (check in - check out )',' Federation Staff flow\r\nAll staff endpoints are shared with the society staff-attendance engine and live under /api/society/staffattendance. There is NO separate /federation/... mount — the fedration_security role is authorized on these paths, and the guard\'s token (federationId set, societyId null) forces every call into its federation branch. So these ARE the federation flow; they just ride the shared engine.\r\nCore rule (who a fed guard can check in): The fed guard fully checks in/out the FEDERATION\'s OWN staff only. Calling check-in on a SOCIETY staff member returns 403 — society staff must instead be recorded via \'Arrived at Federation Gate\', and the society guard completes their check-in. (And the gate-arrival endpoint rejects federation staff: \'check them in directly\'.)\r\n\r\nCase A — the federation\'s OWN staff (full check-in / check-out)\r\nList federation staff (pick a member)\r\nGET  /society/staffattendance/staff/staff-list\r\nAuth role: society_security / fedration_security\r\nFor a fed guard this returns FEDERATION-OWNED staff only (society staff are excluded).\r\nREQUEST\r\nField		Type / notes\r\nsearch	optional	string\r\npage / limit	optional	int — default 1 / 10, max 100\r\nfromDate / toDate	optional	YYYY-MM-DD — attendance range\r\nonlyActive	optional	bool\r\n\r\nRESPONSE • DATA (PAGINATED ARRAY)\r\n{ \"data\": [ {\r\n  \"id\": \"...\", \"name\": \"...\", \"mobile\": \"...\", \"gender\": \"...\", \"photo\": \"<url>\",\r\n  \"societyId\": null, \"federationId\": \"...\", \"serviceTypeName\": \"Guard\",\r\n  \"flats\": [ { \"id\": \"...\", \"flatNumber\": \"A-101\" } ],\r\n  \"attendance\": [ { \"date\": \"2026-07-25\", \"checkInTime\": \"...\", \"checkOutTime\": null,\r\n                    \"checkInType\": \"...\", \"isPresent\": true, \"isCheckedOut\": false, \"workingHours\": 2.5 } ],\r\n  \"dutyStatus\": \"ON_DUTY\", \"isInside\": true,\r\n  \"lastCheckIn\": \"...\", \"lastCheckOut\": null, \"isActive\": true\r\n} ],\r\n  \"pagination\": { \"currentPage\": 1, \"totalPages\": 2, \"totalItems\": 15, \"pageSize\": 10 } }\r\nStaff details\r\nGET  /society/staffattendance/staff/details/:id\r\nAuth role: society_security / fedration_security\r\nPath param id (uuid). Query: date (optional, YYYY-MM-DD). Federation-own staff only.\r\nRESPONSE • DATA\r\n{ \"id\": \"...\", \"name\": \"...\", \"mobile\": \"...\", \"photo\": \"<url>\", \"serviceTypeName\": \"Guard\",\r\n  \"flats\": [ { \"id\": \"...\", \"flatNumber\": \"A-101\" } ],\r\n  \"attendance\": [ { \"date\": \"2026-07-25\", \"checkInTime\": \"...\", \"checkOutTime\": null, \"workingHours\": 2.5 } ],\r\n  \"isInside\": true, \"dutyStatus\": \"ON_DUTY\", \"lastCheckIn\": \"...\", \"lastCheckOut\": null, \"isActive\": true }\r\nCheck in\r\nPOST  /society/staffattendance/staff/checkin/:id\r\nAuth role: society_security / fedration_security\r\nPath param id (uuid). Fed guard: allowed for federation staff (403 for society staff). 400 if already checked in.\r\nRESPONSE • DATA — THE ATTENDANCE RECORD\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"...\", \"staffId\": \"...\", \"societyId\": null, \"date\": \"2026-07-25\",\r\n  \"checkInTime\": \"...\", \"checkOutTime\": null, \"checkInType\": \"...\", \"isManual\": false,\r\n  \"federationArrivedAt\": null, \"federationArrivedBy\": null\r\n}\r\n// meta.message: \"Staff checked in successfully\"\r\nCheck out\r\nPOST  /society/staffattendance/staff/checkout/:id\r\nAuth role: society_security / fedration_security\r\nPath param id (uuid). 400 \'No active check-in found\' if not currently in.\r\nRESPONSE • DATA — THE ATTENDANCE RECORD\r\n{ \"id\": \"...\", \"staffId\": \"...\", \"date\": \"2026-07-25\",\r\n  \"checkInTime\": \"...\", \"checkOutTime\": \"...\", \"checkOutType\": \"...\", \"isManual\": false }\r\n// meta.message: \"Staff checked out successfully\"\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,13,3,'2026-07-30 05:10:32','2026-09-02 11:02:57','2026-07-30',0,NULL,NULL,1937,1,2,0,'2026-09-02 11:02:57'),(1938,1,7,'Export--> Need one refresh button here to refresh the selected data.','<img style=\"width: 1571px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301048-7tlbx.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-07-30 05:19:32','2026-07-30 07:01:54',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1938,1,2,0,'2026-07-30 07:01:54'),(1939,1,1,'federation - If a society is under a Federation, Federation Security should only have the \"Arrived at Gate\" action. The Society Security should handle the complete staff management process, including Check-In and Check-Out for all staff. ','society staff at the federation gate (arrival only)\r\nRecord staff arrival at the fed gate\r\nPOST  /society/staffattendance/staff/federation-gate-arrived/:id\r\nAuth role: fedration_security only\r\nPath param id = society staff uuid. Idempotent. Rejects federation-own staff (use check-in) and staff with no society. Records arrival; the society guard completes the check-in later (that check-in finds and completes this same row).\r\nRESPONSE • DATA — THE ATTENDANCE RECORD\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"...\", \"staffId\": \"...\", \"societyId\": \"...\", \"date\": \"2026-07-25\",\r\n  \"checkInTime\": \"...(provisional)\", \"checkInType\": \"FEDERATION_GATE\",\r\n  \"federationArrivedAt\": \"...\", \"federationArrivedBy\": \"<guardUserId>\"\r\n}\r\n// meta.message: \"Arrival at federation gate recorded. Society security will complete the check-in.\"\r\nNote: the fed guard\'s staff-list returns only federation-own staff, so the society staffId for arrival is obtained from another surface (e.g. QR scan / search).\r\nMonitoring\r\nCurrently inside\r\nGET  /society/staffattendance/staff/currently-inside\r\nAuth role: society_security / fedration_security\r\nQuery: search, page, limit (optional). Fed guard sees federation-own staff plus mapped-society staff currently inside.\r\nRESPONSE • DATA (PAGINATED)\r\n{ \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"...\", \"name\": \"...\", \"mobile\": \"...\", \"photo\": \"<url>\",\r\n  \"serviceTypeName\": \"Guard\", \"flats\": [ { \"id\": \"...\", \"flatNumber\": \"A-101\" } ],\r\n  \"isInside\": true, \"lastCheckIn\": \"...\", \"lastCheckOut\": null } ],\r\n  \"pagination\": { \"currentPage\": 1, \"totalPages\": 1, \"totalItems\": 3, \"pageSize\": 10 } }\r\nStaff dashboard (counts)\r\nGET  /society/staffattendance/staff/dashboard\r\nAuth role: society_security / fedration_security\r\nQuery: date (optional). Fed guard = strict federation scope.\r\nRESPONSE • DATA\r\n{ \"total\": 15, \"arrivedToday\": 9, \"insideToday\": 6, \"checkedOutToday\": 3, \"pendingArrival\": 6 }\r\nAlso authorized but SOCIETY-scoped (they key off societyId, which a fed guard token does not carry, so they return empty for a fed guard — listed only for completeness): GET /attendance/date, GET /attendance/staff/:id, GET /attendance/summary.\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,8,'2026-07-30 05:20:48','2026-09-10 11:56:20',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1939,1,2,0,'2026-09-10 11:56:20'),(1940,1,7,'Export--> Click on the load records to select --> but there is n serial number column.','<img style=\"width: 1576px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301051-3jbm8.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-07-30 05:22:48','2026-08-03 05:40:15',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1940,1,2,0,'2026-08-03 05:40:15'),(1941,1,7,'Export--> Give teh pagignation like shown teh page numbers to select teh respective page.','**\r\n<img style=\"width: 1568px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301052-s5skk.png\"><br>\r\n**',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-07-30 05:23:21','2026-08-03 05:40:25',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1941,1,2,0,'2026-08-03 05:40:25'),(1942,1,7,'Export → When I select “Select all on this page,” it only selects 50 records. I need the option to select up to 100 records. Currently, there is no pagination option (like selecting 100 or 200 records), and no checkbox to select records across pages.','\r\nPlease add a more user-friendly pagination and selection feature.\r\n\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 1580px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301054-2xc9d.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-07-30 05:27:19','2026-08-03 07:29:51',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1942,1,2,0,'2026-08-03 07:29:51'),(1943,1,1,'federation visitor flow ','The setup\r\nThink of a federation as a big gated township that contains several societies (buildings/complexes) inside it. So there are two gates a visitor must pass:\r\n\r\nGate 1 – Federation main gate (outer) → manned by a federation guard\r\nGate 2 – Society gate (inner) → manned by the society\'s own guard\r\nIf a society is not in a federation, there\'s just one gate (its own).\r\n\r\nThe normal visitor journey (step by step)\r\nStep 1 — Visitor reaches the federation main gate.\r\nThe federation guard notes down the visitor (name, whom they\'re visiting, etc.). The society\'s own guard is not allowed to add visitors here — if they try, the app stops them and says \"entries are handled at the federation gate.\"\r\n\r\nStep 2 — The system decides: allowed straight in, or needs permission?\r\n\r\nIf it\'s a type that can go directly (say a known/allowed visitor) → marked Approved.\r\nOtherwise → marked Pending, and a request is sent to the resident.\r\nStep 3 — The resident approves or rejects (on their phone).\r\nThe resident is always the one who decides who reaches their door. They tap Approve or Reject.\r\n\r\nStep 4 — Visitor walks to the society gate.\r\nThe society guard sees the approved visitor and taps \"Arrived at Society.\" Now the visitor is officially inside. Only the society\'s own guard can press this button.\r\n\r\nThat\'s the full path:\r\nFederation gate (logged) → Resident approves → Society gate (arrived).\r\n\r\nIf the resident pre-approves in advance\r\nSometimes a resident adds a visitor before they arrive (\"my guest is coming at 6pm\").\r\n\r\nOn a federation society, that heads-up goes to the federation guards (not the society guard).\r\nWhen the guest reaches the main gate, the federation guard lets them in, and the society guard still confirms arrival at the inner gate.\r\nIf a visit is cancelled\r\nA guard can cancel a visitor with a reason. The visitor then shows as \"Cancelled\" — it stays visible in the history (it is not hidden/deleted), so everyone can see it was cancelled.\r\n\r\nOne important behind-the-scenes rule (why it matters)\r\nWhen the resident approves, the visitor\'s label changes from \"Pending\" to \"Approved\" — even if they\'re still standing at the outer gate. So the system does not trust the label to know where the visitor physically is. Instead it uses timestamps:\r\n\r\n\"Entered the federation gate at ___\" (set once, never changes)\r\n\"Arrived at the society at ___\" (set once, never changes)\r\nSo a dashboard counts \"at federation gate\" vs \"arrived at society\" using those two time-stamps, not the changing label.\r\n\r\nWho uses which app\r\nFederation guard app → logs visitors at the main gate, sees all societies\' visitor counts, admits pre-approved guests.\r\nSociety guard app → for a federation society, only confirms \"Arrived at Society.\"\r\nResident app → approve/reject, and pre-approve guests.\r\nSimple summary in one line\r\nFor a federation society: visitor is logged at the federation\'s main gate → resident approves on their phone → society\'s guard confirms arrival. \r\n\r\n\r\nFederation Security — Visitor APIs\r\nBase URL: /api/visitormanagement\r\nAuth: every call needs the guard\'s JWT in the header → Authorization: Bearer <token>. The federation is read from the token, never sent in the body.\r\nRoles: Federation guard token = role fedration_security. Society guard token = role society_security.\r\nResponse shape (all endpoints): { success, message, data }. Errors come back with a proper HTTP status + { success:false, message }.\r\n\r\nThe flow (order of calls)\r\nGuard opens app → ① get societies (home) and ② get visitors (dashboard).\r\nVisitor arrives → ③ log visitor at federation gate (search resident first with ⑤/⑥).\r\nIf visitor was pre-approved by a resident → ④ admit pre-approved.\r\nResident approves/rejects on the resident app (not the guard app).\r\nVisitor reaches the society → ⑦ society guard taps \"Arrived at Society\".\r\nAnytime → ⑧ view a visitor\'s full timeline.\r\n① Home screen — societies with live counts\r\nGET /federation-gate/societies — (federation guard)\r\nNo input.\r\nReturns: federationId, totalSocieties, and societies[], each card:\r\nsocietyId, societyName, city, state, address, totalVisitorsToday, atFederationGate, arrivedAtSociety, pendingApproval.\r\n\r\n② Visitor dashboard (across the federation)\r\nGET /federation-gate/visitors — (federation guard)\r\nQuery (all optional): societyId, status, search, fromDate (YYYY-MM-DD), toDate, federationOriginOnly (true/false), page, limit (max 100).\r\nReturns: a paginated list of visitors with their details + status + gate timestamps.\r\n\r\n③ Log a visitor at the federation (outer) gate\r\nPOST /federation-gate/visitors — (federation guard)\r\nSend as multipart/form-data (so photos can be attached).\r\nBody:\r\n\r\nfield	required	notes\r\nsocietyId	✅	which society the visitor is going to\r\nvisitorTypeId	✅	visitor category (guest/delivery/etc.)\r\nname	✅	1–150 chars\r\nmobile	✅	6–15 chars\r\nflatId	optional	target flat\r\nresidentId	optional	target resident\r\npurpose	optional	≤255 chars\r\nvehicleNo	optional	≤50 chars\r\ncompanyId	optional	for delivery/company visitors\r\nscheduledVisitDate	optional	ISO date\r\nimages	optional	up to 5 photo files\r\nReturns (201): the created visitor record. It\'s treated like a normal entry (auto-approved or sent to the resident as pending) and the society/resident is notified.\r\n\r\n④ Admit a pre-approved visitor\r\nPOST /federation-gate/visitors/:id/admit-preapproved — (federation guard)\r\n:id = visitor id (UUID). No body.\r\nUse this when a resident pre-approved a guest and they show up at the gate. Marks them Approved and stamps the federation gate-in time. (Society guard still confirms arrival later.)\r\n\r\n⑤ Search residents/flats (to pick who the visitor is visiting)\r\nGET /federation-gate/residents/search — (federation guard)\r\nQuery: search (name/flat, optional, ≤100), societyId (optional).\r\nReturns: matching residents with their flat info — use the ids in call ③.\r\n\r\n⑥ Full resident directory (browse)\r\nGET /federation-gate/residents/directory — (federation guard)\r\nQuery: search, societyId, page, limit.\r\nReturns: paginated directory (societies → residents → flats/family/tenants).\r\n\r\n⑦ \"Arrived at Society\" — society guard only\r\nPOST /federation-gate/visitors/:id/arrived — (society guard, society_security)\r\n:id = visitor id. No body.\r\nThe society\'s own guard presses this when the visitor physically reaches the society. Stamps arrival time and moves status to ARRIVED_AT_SOCIETY. Federation guards are not allowed to call this.\r\n\r\n⑧ Visitor timeline (history)\r\nGET /federation-gate/visitors/:id/timeline — (either guard)\r\n:id = visitor id.\r\nReturns: the full ordered event log (logged at gate → approved/declined → arrived), each with actor type, actor name, time, and note.\r\n\r\nHandled by other apps (for context — not the Federation Security app)\r\nResident approves/rejects a visitor: resident app → PUT /visitor/approve-request/:id, PUT /visitor/reject-request/:id.\r\nResident pre-approves a guest: POST /visitormanagement/resident/create-preapprove-visitor.\r\nCancel a visitor request (with reason): PUT /visitor/:id/cancel-visitor-request.\r\nVisitor statuses the app will see\r\nPENDING (waiting for resident), APPROVED, DECLINED, PREAPPROVED, ARRIVED_AT_SOCIETY, CANCELLED, EXPIRED.\r\n👉 Important for the developer: to show where the visitor physically is, rely on the timestamps (federationCheckInAt, societyArrivedAt), not on status — because when the resident approves, the status flips to APPROVED even while the visitor is still at the federation gate. \"Pending approval\" should be judged by isApproved = false, not status = PENDING.',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,5,'2026-07-30 05:46:11','2026-09-10 13:12:30',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1943,1,2,0,'2026-09-10 13:12:30'),(1944,1,7,'How to verify the Preview screen before publishing imported records. here in the excel file only previews the data.','Verify the Preview screen before publishing imported records.',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-07-30 06:05:30','2026-07-30 12:44:44',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1944,1,2,0,'2026-07-30 12:44:44'),(1945,1,1,'app - treasurer','issue - There are issues in the Resident Mobile App when a resident is assigned multiple flats.\r\n\r\nFor example, if a resident has Flat X with a ₹1500 Due and Flat Y with a ₹1500 Advance, only the Advance for the active flat is displayed. The Due amount for the other flat is not shown anywhere. Additionally, in the My Ledger section, the ledger entries of both flats are merged together when viewing the active flat.\r\n\r\nPlease fix this so that each flat maintains its own independent Advance, Due, and Ledger. When the user switches the active flat, only the balances and ledger entries for that selected flat should be displayed.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOn the three \"money\" screens, send the currently-selected flat\'s flatId in the request body. That\'s it — the backend now uses it to show only that flat\'s data.\r\n\r\nWhich API calls to update\r\nAdd \"flatId\": \"<active flat id>\" to the body of these POST calls:\r\n\r\nScreen	API\r\nHome / Dashboard (Due, Advance, etc.)	POST /dashboard/summary\r\nOutstanding balance (Due + Advance)	POST /ledger/outstanding\r\nMy Ledger (transaction history)	POST /ledger/statement\r\nExample body:\r\n\r\n\r\n{ \"flatId\": \"the-flat-the-user-currently-has-selected\" }\r\n(keep whatever other fields you already send — just add flatId).\r\n\r\nWhen to send it\r\nSend the flat the user currently has selected (the same flat you already use for the Invoices screen).\r\nWhen the user switches the active flat, call these APIs again with the new flatId and refresh the screens. Each flat will then show its own Due, Advance, and ledger — nothing merged.\r\nWhat happens now\r\nFull advance covers the flat → that flat shows the advance; the other flat\'s Due shows separately under its own flat.\r\nSwitch flat → balances and ledger instantly change to that flat only.\r\nIf you don\'t send flatId, the backend falls back to the resident\'s stored active flat — but to be safe and correct, always send the selected flatId explicitly.\r\nNothing else changes\r\nSame endpoints, same response format — just one extra field in the request.\r\nNo new screens, no app-store-blocking changes.\r\nIt only works after the backend is deployed to the test server, so coordinate the timing with the backend deploy.\r\nQuick test to confirm it works\r\nUse a resident who has two flats — one with a Due, one with an Advance:\r\n\r\nSelect Flat X → should show only Flat X\'s Due; My Ledger shows only Flat X entries.\r\nSwitch to Flat Y → should show only Flat Y\'s Advance; My Ledger shows only Flat Y entries.\r\nIf each flat shows its own numbers (not blended), it\'s working.',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,4,'2026-07-30 06:28:00','2026-09-04 08:39:28',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1945,1,2,0,'2026-09-04 08:39:28'),(1946,1,1,'app - treasurer','issue - There are inconsistencies between the Treasurer Web and Treasurer Mobile App dashboards.\r\n\r\nThe dashboard values and Monthly Snapshot data shown in the mobile app do not match the values displayed on the web. Please ensure that both platforms display the same data and calculations.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the mobile app dashboard is missing the Advances, Bills, and Expenses Summary sections that are available on the web. Please add these sections to the mobile app to match the web dashboard.\r\n\r\nAlso, remove the Monthly Trend section from the Treasurer Mobile App dashboard, as it is no longer required. Ensure the dashboard UI and data remain consistent across both the Web Application and the Mobile App.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe 2 rules to follow\r\n1. Income = Total Maintenance Collected (money actually received)\r\n\r\nRead the field totalIncome and show that as Income.\r\n❌ Do NOT use totalIncomeInvoiced — that\'s the \"billed\" amount and is what made mobile differ from web.\r\nIn the Monthly Snapshot, use the collected income too, and calculate Net = Income − Expenses yourself in the app (don\'t use the server\'s netBalance).\r\n2. Outstanding = Total Invoiced − Total Collected\r\n\r\nRead the field outstandingDues and show that as Outstanding. (It already equals invoiced minus collected — nothing to calculate.)\r\nEverything you need to do, in order\r\nIncome card → show totalIncome (collected). Remove any use of totalIncomeInvoiced.\r\nOutstanding card → show outstandingDues.\r\nMonthly Snapshot → Income = collected income; Net = Income − Expenses (calculated in the app); use the current month window.\r\nSend the same date filter to every dashboard call that web sends (year/month or date range).\r\nAdd the 3 missing sections by calling:\r\nAdvances → GET /api/app-treasurer/advance/dashboard\r\nBills → GET /api/app-treasurer/bills/dashboard\r\nExpenses Summary → GET /api/app-treasurer/expenses/paid-dashboard\r\nRemove the Monthly Trend section → stop calling GET /api/app-treasurer/dashboard/monthly-trend.\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,13,3,'2026-07-30 06:55:02','2026-09-02 10:33:34',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1946,1,2,0,'2026-09-02 10:33:34'),(1947,1,1,'Treasurer App--> Reports--> Select the future fianancial year--> it should not be shows the data, because for the future there is no data.','<img style=\"width: 424px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301233-4bub2.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,7,5,'2026-07-30 07:03:39','2026-09-01 11:22:47',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1947,1,2,0,'2026-09-01 11:22:47'),(1948,1,1,'Treasurer App--> Reports--> For excel, pdf and csv--> Shown the above error.','<img style=\"width: 291px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301234-pdhb9.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-07-30 07:04:42','2026-08-31 07:26:34',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1948,1,2,0,'2026-08-31 07:26:34'),(1949,1,1,'app - treasurer','issue -The Financial Reports dashboard values are also different between the web and the mobile app. Please verify the calculations and ensure the reports are consistent across both platforms.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n Make the mobile Reports read the same fields and same period as web:\r\n\r\nIncome = collected (cash) everywhere a single Income/Net figure is shown:\r\nReports dashboard → use totalIncomeReceived (fall back to totalIncome). ❌ don\'t use totalIncomeInvoiced.\r\nAnnual Summary → use totalIncomeReceived; compute Net = income − expenses in the app.\r\nOutstanding → use outstandingDues (already = Invoiced − Collected).\r\nSend the same period params the web sends (same year, same month/range). Two gotchas that are the same on both platforms but cause confusion if one app relies on defaults:\r\nMost report endpoints default to the financial year when no month is sent.\r\nThe income-overview endpoint defaults to the calendar year — send an explicit year if you use it, so both platforms match.\r\nFor the Monthly table/chart, it\'s fine to keep showing both \"Expected/Invoiced\" and \"Received\" columns (both apps should show the same two), since that view is a comparison — just make sure the headline Income/Net tiles use the collected figure.',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,13,3,'2026-07-30 07:06:53','2026-08-31 07:25:51',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1949,1,2,0,'2026-08-31 07:25:51'),(1950,1,1,'app - treasurer','issue - There is an issue in the Treasurer Payment Management module.\r\n\r\nIf a resident owns two flats, and a payment is recorded from the Admin/Treasurer for one specific flat, the payment is incorrectly reflected as cleared for both flats.\r\n\r\nPlease fix this so that payments are always mapped to the correct flat only. Each flat should maintain its own independent payment history, outstanding dues, advance balance, and ledger. Recording or clearing a payment for one flat must not affect the financial records of any other flat owned by the same resident. Ensure this behaviour is consistent across both the Web Application and the Mobile App.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSend the selected flat\'s flatId in the request body of POST /payment/list (same as you now do for invoices, outstanding, ledger, and dashboard). When the user switches the active flat, re-fetch with the new flatId → each flat shows only its own payments. If flatId is omitted, it falls back to showing all ',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,6,'2026-07-30 07:19:27','2026-09-02 11:30:43',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1950,1,2,0,'2026-09-02 11:30:43'),(1951,1,1,'As mentionbed by savita, if resident and the treasurer mobile numbers are the same, then ths is occured, please check the same.','<img style=\"width: 299px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301248-ydvea.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-07-30 07:19:40','2026-08-31 07:23:49',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1951,1,2,0,'2026-08-31 07:23:49'),(1952,1,1,'Treasurer App--> Reports--> Alignment is not getting proper for the months.','<img style=\"width: 302px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301403-q1vub.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,7,5,'2026-07-30 08:34:44','2026-09-01 13:08:36',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1952,1,2,0,'2026-09-01 13:08:36'),(1953,1,1,'Treasurer App--> Reports--> For all the categories, the reports is not get downloaded.','<img style=\"width: 317px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301405-v174o.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,7,7,'2026-07-30 08:35:49','2026-09-02 11:25:33',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1953,1,2,0,'2026-09-02 11:25:33'),(1954,1,1,'Treasurer App--> Adjust the spacing.','<img style=\"width: 301px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301406-nlfwo.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-07-30 08:36:27','2026-08-31 07:08:16',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1954,1,2,0,'2026-08-31 07:08:16'),(1955,1,1,'Treasurer App-->Reports--> Message shown reports downloaded but actually it shown line this and unable to open.','<img style=\"width: 314px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301406-knwz7.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,7,8,'2026-07-30 08:37:23','2026-09-02 11:23:55',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1955,1,2,0,'2026-09-02 11:23:55'),(1956,1,7,'Export--> exported excel file--> Image should be bydefault hyperlink, user clicks on image hyperlink and directly opens the image. ','<img style=\"width: 1599px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301656-2uzhb.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,9,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-07-30 11:29:09','2026-08-03 05:49:48',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1956,1,2,0,'2026-08-03 05:49:48'),(1957,1,1,'In Federation → Society, the opening balance should be visible in the listing. Also, the word \"Avigo Admin\" is appearing twice—please remove the duplicate.','<img style=\"width: 1561px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607301736-53wtt.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-07-30 12:06:57','2026-08-10 11:52:44',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1957,1,2,0,'2026-08-10 11:52:44'),(1958,1,1,'Federation--> Do the needful chnages as you discussed with me like transfer the federation admin menu to the registered users menu.','<img style=\"width: 1573px;\"