Rent out--> New--> Same validations changes applied here, please correct all the validation changes. ','<img style=\"width: 1575px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131714-pxicf.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 11:44:14','2026-08-27 11:02:08',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2221,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:02:08'),(2222,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Shop--> Rent out--> New--> What happens if agreement date missed, which scenario happens.','<img style=\"width: 1560px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131719-opuwl.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 11:49:43','2026-08-27 11:03:56',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2222,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:03:56'),(2223,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Shop--> Rent out--> New--> Common in all forms--> GIve mandatory asterisk for all forms, which fieklds are mandatory.','<img style=\"width: 1567px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131720-9loqq.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 11:50:41','2026-08-27 11:04:46',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2223,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:04:46'),(2224,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Shop--> Rent out--> New-->All--> Common issue, in the pagignation, please check that if i goes to the second page, then the numbering starts with 11 instead of 1.','<img style=\"width: 1591px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131722-ngqpv.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 11:52:56','2026-08-27 11:05:10',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2224,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:05:10'),(2225,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Shop--> Rent out--> New--> No validations are there.','<img style=\"width: 1594px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131736-fnbed.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 12:06:57','2026-08-27 11:05:36',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2225,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:05:36'),(2226,1,1,'Resident App - Credit Note - see in description','Suppose we initially send a ₹1,500 invoice to a resident, but later we realize that the actual amount should have been ₹1,000. If the ₹1,500 invoice has not yet been paid, and we create a credit note for ₹500, the resident’s invoice should be updated from ₹1,500 to ₹1,000.\r\n\r\nIf the ₹1,500 invoice has already been paid, the invoice should remain ₹1,500, and the ₹500 credit amount should be added as an advance for that resident.\r\n\r\n\r\nInvoices that carry a credit note\r\nA credit note corrects an invoice after it was issued. Example: a resident was billed ₹1,500 but the correct amount was ₹1,000, so the treasurer raises a ₹500 credit note.\r\nThe agreed rule\r\nThe invoice amount is never rewritten — it stays ₹1,500, because the credit note is the auditable record of the correction. What changes is the amount owed.\r\nSITUATION	INVOICE	PAID	CREDIT NOTE	NOW OWED	EXTRA\r\nNot yet paid	1,500	0	500	1,000	—\r\nAlready paid in full	1,500	1,500	500	0	₹500 advance created for the resident\r\nIn the second case the backend automatically creates an advance the moment the credit note is posted. It appears in the resident’s existing advances list and is consumed by their next invoice. No app work is needed for the advance — just be aware the money shows up there rather than as a refund.\r\nENDPOINTS\r\n POST   /api/app-resident/invoice/list\r\n POST   /api/app-resident/invoice/getbyid   body: { \"id\": \"<invoiceId>\" }\r\nNEW FIELDS ON EVERY INVOICE\r\n{\r\n  \"id\":        \"...\",\r\n  \"invoiceNo\": \"INV-1786621766514\",\r\n  \"status\":    \"POSTED\",\r\n \r\n  \"totalAmount\":    1500,   // original billed amount - unchanged\r\n  \"paidAmount\":        0,\r\n  \"creditedAmount\":  500,   // NEW - credit notes applied\r\n  \"balanceDue\":     1000,   // NEW - what the resident actually owes\r\n \r\n  \"penaltyAmount\":     0,\r\n  \"isPayable\":      true    // meaning changed - see below\r\n}\r\nFIELD	USE IT FOR\r\nbalanceDue  NEW	The amount owed. Already equals totalAmount − paidAmount − creditedAmount, clamped at 0. Show this wherever you currently show an amount due.\r\ncreditedAmount  NEW	Show a “Credited” row only when > 0, so ordinary invoices keep their current layout.\r\ntotalAmount	Still the invoice’s headline value. Do not subtract anything from it yourself.\r\nisPayable	Whether to show the Pay button. Now false once nothing is left to collect.\r\nWHAT THE RESIDENT SHOULD SEE\r\nNOW (WRONG)\r\nTotal Amount	₹1,500\r\nAmount Paid	₹0\r\nBalance Due	₹1,500\r\nREQUIRED\r\nTotal Amount	₹1,500\r\nAmount Paid	₹0\r\nCredited (Credit Note)	₹500\r\nBalance Due	₹1,000\r\nThis is the same layout the downloadable invoice PDF already uses, so the screen and the PDF will agree.\r\nWhy isPayable matters\r\nA credit note does not change invoice status — a fully credited invoice stays POSTED. So a status check alone still makes it look payable. isPayable now also requires a remaining balance, so trust it rather than testing status yourself.\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,10,'2026-08-13 12:24:23','2026-09-16 07:01:45',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2226,1,2,0,'2026-09-16 07:01:45'),(2227,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Shop--> Sale--> New --> HEre is the Month of Possession is correct title instead of the Date of possession, also months are only twelve so no need to give master for this with other option.','<img style=\"width: 1562px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131758-v4yvu.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,4,'2026-08-13 12:29:12','2026-08-27 11:11:54',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2227,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:11:54'),(2228,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Shop--> Sale--> Resale --> No validatons applied here for the form, in alue, diamensions, pricing.','<img style=\"width: 1540px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608131813-eqn0a.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 12:43:25','2026-08-27 11:17:53',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2228,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:17:53'),(2229,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Row House --> Lease Out--> Resale --> No validatons applied here for the form.','',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-13 13:05:25','2026-08-27 11:33:02',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2229,1,2,0,'2026-08-27 11:33:02'),(2230,1,12,'Inventory Properties--> Row House --> Lease Out--> New--> Common issues in all that added pereviously forms sam