367,1,2,0,'2026-09-01 06:51:39'),(2368,1,12,'Reports--> Filters--> If i am selecting the Hotel then its only related transaction types open, so there is less confusion. and gets the accurate and perfect data.','<img style=\"width: 1573px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608181728-ipe22.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,3,'2026-08-18 11:59:00','2026-08-25 11:35:21',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2368,1,2,0,'2026-08-25 11:35:21'),(2369,1,12,'Common in all Reports--> Selected filters have no data. so please check all reports in your side and correct it.','<img style=\"width: 1577px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608181731-0kqaw.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,14,2,NULL,7,7,'2026-08-18 12:03:21','2026-08-29 11:58:34',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2369,1,2,0,'2026-08-29 11:58:34'),(2370,1,1,'Treasurer App - Line Items',' Add a \"Default Account\" dropdown below Category. Load it with:\r\n\r\nGET /api/app-treasurer/accounts?type=INCOME&isActive=true&limit=1000&billable=true\r\nSwap INCOME for EXPENSE depending on the selected category\'s type. The category list already returns a type field.\r\n\r\n2. Clear the account when the category type changes, exactly as the web does.\r\n\r\n3. Send it as defaultAccountId in the create/update body:\r\n\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"name\": \"Clubhouse Charges\",\r\n  \"categoryId\": \"...\",\r\n  \"defaultAccountId\": \"...\",\r\n  \"defaultRate\": 500,\r\n  \"gstApplicable\": true,\r\n  \"gstPercentage\": 18,\r\n  \"description\": \"...\"\r\n}\r\n4. Remove the \"Line Item Code\" field — there is no such column, so anything typed there is discarded. Either drop it or tell me and I\'ll add the column properly.\r\n\r\nEndpoints (unchanged, already exist):\r\n\r\n\r\nGET    /api/app-treasurer/masters/line-items\r\nPOST   /api/app-treasurer/masters/line-items\r\nPUT    /api/app-treasurer/masters/line-items/:id\r\nDELETE /api/app-treasurer/masters/line-items/:id',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,4,'2026-08-21 07:04:49','2026-09-01 11:14:08',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2370,1,2,0,'2026-09-01 11:14:08'),(2371,1,1,'Treasurer App - Create Expenses - account , amount is not fetching like admin compare admin and app for create expenses.same check for create invoices also.','When a line item is selected, fill three things from the selected master object:\r\n\r\n1. Rate ← master.defaultRate\r\n\r\n2. Account ← master.defaultAccountId\r\n\r\nSelect that account in the dropdown. Guard it the way the web does — only pre-select it if the id is present in the loaded account list; otherwise leave the field blank so the user picks one. Never leave whatever was previously selected sitting there, which is how \"Water Charges\" appeared.\r\n\r\n3. GST ← master.gstPercentage, as described earlier (only when the society GST switch is on, split in half for CGST/SGST).\r\n\r\nThen compute:\r\nAmount = Rate × Quantity\r\nand recompute whenever either changes.\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 2127px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608211459-npsuk.png\"><br>\r\n<img style=\"width: 466px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608211500-xntbd.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,13,2,NULL,13,9,'2026-08-21 09:30:08','2026-09-03 13:23:25',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2371,1,2,0,'2026-09-03 13:23:25'),(2372,1,1,'Treasurer App - Flat Ledger - only pdf option is there for export. show all three options pdf excel csv.','Turn the single download button into a menu with three options, exactly like the web, and send the choice in the request body:\r\n\r\n\r\nPOST /api/app-treasurer/flat-ledger/summary/export\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"format\": \"pdf\" | \"excel\" | \"csv\",\r\n\r\n  \"search\":     \"...\",   // optional — keep the current filters\r\n  \"status\":     \"...\",\r\n  \"buildingId\": \"...\",\r\n  \"wingId\":     \"...\",\r\n  \"flatId\":     \"...\"\r\n}\r\nPass whatever filters are active on screen, so the export matches what the user is looking at.\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 451px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608211524-i5zwm.png\"><br>\r\n',NULL,NULL,5,8,2,NULL,13,7,'2026-08-21 09:54:45','2026-09-04 10:51:16',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,2372,1,2,0,'2026-09-04 10:51:16'),(23