,1920,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-30 12:42:41','2026-07-30 12:42:41',NULL,0),(4821,1944,'Issue',9,'','2026-07-30 12:44:31','2026-07-30 12:44:31',NULL,0),(4822,1944,'Issue',7,'','2026-07-30 12:44:44','2026-07-30 12:44:44',NULL,0),(4823,1922,'Issue',9,'','2026-07-30 12:44:49','2026-07-30 12:44:49',NULL,0),(4824,1905,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-30 12:47:07','2026-07-30 12:47:07',NULL,0),(4825,1869,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-30 13:12:06','2026-07-30 13:12:06',NULL,0),(4826,1864,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-30 13:12:31','2026-07-30 13:12:31',NULL,0),(4827,1964,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 04:58:33','2026-07-31 04:58:33',NULL,0),(4828,1963,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 05:07:34','2026-07-31 05:07:34',NULL,0),(4829,1962,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 05:19:03','2026-07-31 05:19:03',NULL,0),(4830,1961,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 05:19:43','2026-07-31 05:19:43',NULL,0),(4831,1960,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 05:21:51','2026-07-31 05:21:51',NULL,0),(4832,1891,'Issue',13,'check once then resolve','2026-07-31 05:34:26','2026-07-31 05:34:26',NULL,0),(4833,1896,'Issue',13,'  \"data\": {\r\n    \"summary\": {\r\n      \"totalReceived\": 808,\r\n      \"totalGiven\": 0,\r\n      \"unadjustedBalance\": 808\r\n    }\r\n\r\ncheck this ','2026-07-31 05:45:39','2026-07-31 05:45:39',NULL,0),(4834,1955,'Issue',13,'Reports download shows \"downloaded\" but file is 0 KB / won\'t open\r\n\r\nWhy it happens: The app is giving the report URL to the phone\'s download manager. That download manager doesn\'t send our login token, so the server rejects it and you get a 0-byte file.\r\n\r\nThe fix (backend is ready): do the download in 2 steps.\r\n\r\nStep 1 — Ask the server for a download link (this call must include the login token, like all your other API calls):\r\n\r\n\r\nGET /api/app-treasurer/reports/download?type=annual&format=pdf&year=2026&month=7&delivery=link\r\nHeader: Authorization: Bearer <token>\r\ntype = monthly | income-expense | annual | balance-sheet | reconciliation\r\nformat = pdf | xlsx | csv\r\nmonth = optional (leave it out for the whole year)\r\ndelivery=link is the important new part — always add it\r\nYou get back this:\r\n\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"success\": true,\r\n  \"data\": {\r\n    \"downloadUrl\": \"https://....s3....?X-Amz-Signature=....\",\r\n    \"fileName\": \"annual_2026.pdf\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\nStep 2 — Download data.downloadUrl.\r\nGive that URL to the download manager / open it. Do NOT add the token to this one — it already works by itself. The link is valid for about 10 minutes.\r\n\r\nIn short:\r\n\r\n❌ Old (broken): give /reports/download directly to the download manager.\r\n✅ New: call /reports/download?...&delivery=link with the token → get downloadUrl → download that (no token).\r\nDo this for all report types and all 3 formats (PDF, Excel, CSV) — same flow.','2026-07-31 05:59:35','2026-07-31 05:59:35',NULL,0),(4835,1953,'Issue',13,'check once then resolve','2026-07-31 06:05:46','2026-07-31 06:05:46',NULL,0),(4836,1916,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 06:06:34','2026-07-31 06:06:34',NULL,0),(4837,1948,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 06:09:09','2026-07-31 06:09:09',NULL,0),(4838,1947,'Issue',13,'disable future years and dates','2026-07-31 06:10:05','2026-07-31 06:10:05',NULL,0),(4839,1918,'Issue',13,'The backend blocks it, but the app currently only finds out after the user taps Submit. To warn them before submit, add this simple check in the journal form:\r\n\r\nBefore allowing submit, collect the accounts used on debit lines and the accounts used on credit lines. If any account appears in both, show an inline error and block submit:\r\n\"The same account cannot be used for both debit and credit.\"','2026-07-31 06:13:24','2026-07-31 06:13:24',NULL,0),(4840,1903,'Issue',13,'check once then resolve','2026-07-31 06:19:39','2026-07-31 06:19:39',NULL,0),(4841,1968,'Issue',7,'<img style=\"width: 1274px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607311149-mjnrd.png\"><br>\r\n','2026-07-31 06:19:48','2026-07-31 06:19:48',NULL,0),(4842,1908,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 06:24:18','2026-07-31 06:24:18',NULL,0),(4843,1887,'Issue',13,'\r\nWhen the treasurer attaches an image/doc at create time, the app must send it as multipart/form-data to the with-attachment endpoints, with the file field named exactly attachment — not the plain create endpoints:\r\n\r\nAction	Use this (multipart, file field attachment)	❌ Not this\r\nCreate bill + file	POST /app-treasurer/bills/with-attachment	POST /app-treasurer/bills\r\nCreate expense + file	POST /app-treasurer/expenses/with-attachment (new)	POST /app-treasurer/expenses\r\nEdit + replace file	PUT /app-treasurer/{bills|expenses}/:id/with-attachment	—\r\nSend the other fields (amount, vendor, line items, etc.) as normal form fields in the same multipart request. The plain POST /bills / POST /expenses throw the file away — that\'s why nothing showed. Once the app uses the with-attachment routes, the attachment saves and will appear','2026-07-31 06:43:43','2026-07-31 06:43:43',NULL,0),(4844,1972,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 07:31:39','2026-07-31 07:31:39',NULL,0),(4845,1971,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 07:33:39','2026-07-31 07:33:39',NULL,0),(4846,1968,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 08:16:53','2026-07-31 08:16:53',NULL,0),(4847,1899,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 08:38:10','2026-07-31 08:38:10',NULL,0),(4848,1904,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 08:44:20','2026-07-31 08:44:20',NULL,0),(4849,1867,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 08:46:07','2026-07-31 08:46:07',NULL,0),(4850,1851,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 08:46:42','2026-07-31 08:46:42',NULL,0),(4851,1975,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 08:54:42','2026-07-31 08:54:42',NULL,0),(4852,1974,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 09:01:06','2026-07-31 09:01:06',NULL,0),(4853,1672,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 09:01:55','2026-07-31 09:01:55',NULL,0),(4854,1984,'Issue',7,'<img style=\"width: 1580px;\" src=\"clipboard-202607311541-24mgh.png\"><br>\r\n','2026-07-31 10:11:06','2026-07-31 10:11:06',NULL,0),(4855,1988,'Issue',13,'','2026-07-31 10:30:19','2026-07-31 10:30:19',NULL,0),(4856,1992,'Issue',7,'<img style=\"width: 1588px;\" src=\"clipboard-20