),(5576,1875,'Issue',13,'Change the account dropdown on the Create Invoice screen to request\r\nGET /api/app-treasurer/accounts?type=INCOME&isActive=true&limit=1000\r\n\r\nThe same applies to Expenses\r\nExpense line items are the mirror image: they must use EXPENSE accounts, and the backend rejects anything else. The web has a separate fetch for that too. So on the Create Expense screen:\r\nGET /api/app-treasurer/accounts?type=EXPENSE&isActive=true&limit=1000\r\n\r\n\r\nImportant — don\'t apply this everywhere\r\nOnly the line-item account dropdowns should be filtered. The Chart of Accounts screen, journal entries, and payment forms legitimately need all five types. The web code carries this exact warning:\r\nDo NOT reuse this for the Chart of Accounts management page or other forms that legitimately need all types.','2026-08-21 05:30:45','2026-08-21 05:30:45',NULL,0),(5577,1870,'Issue',13,'','2026-08-21 05:39:41','2026-08-21 05:39:41',NULL,0),(5578,2281,'Issue',14,'','2026-08-21 06:28:15','2026-08-21 06:28:15',NULL,0),(5579,1866,'Issue',13,'Step 1 — Get the list of flats\r\n\r\nPOST /api/app-treasurer/flat-ledger/summary\r\nThis gives all flats with their money summary. Show them as cards or a list.\r\n\r\nStep 2 — When a flat is tapped, get its ledger\r\n\r\nPOST /api/app-treasurer/flat-ledger/detail\r\nThe reply has four parts:\r\n\r\nflat — flat number, building, wing, floor\r\nresidents — name, mobile, email\r\nsummary — the numbers for the top tiles\r\ntransactions — the list of all entries\r\nStep 3 — Show five tiles at the top\r\nCopy these exactly from the admin screen, in this order:\r\n\r\nTile	Field to use	Colour\r\nTotal Billed	summary.totalBilled	Blue\r\nTotal Paid	summary.totalPaid	Green\r\nPending	summary.totalPending	Orange\r\nDues (Pending Invoices)	summary.pendingInvoiceCount	Red if more than 0\r\nAdvance Balance	summary.advanceBalance	Purple\r\nThe Advance Balance tile is the important one for your case. If a resident paid ₹1,000 advance and a ₹200 invoice was raised, this field already sends 800. The app does not calculate anything — just show the number.\r\n\r\nStep 4 — Show the transaction table below\r\nSeven columns, same as admin:\r\n\r\n\r\nDate | Type | Reference | Description | Debit | Credit | Balance\r\nUse transactions[] for the rows. Balance is the runningBalance field.\r\n\r\nColour the balance orange when it is more than 0 (money is owed) and green when it is 0 (nothing owed).\r\n\r\nStep 5 — Give each Type a coloured badge\r\nThe type field will be one of these:\r\n\r\nINVOICE — bill raised\r\nPAYMENT — money received\r\nOPENING_BALANCE — old balance carried in\r\nADVANCE_INCOMING — advance money paid\r\nADVANCE_ADJUSTMENT — advance used against an invoice\r\nCREDIT_NOTE — bill reduced\r\nThe ADVANCE_ADJUSTMENT row is what shows the ₹200 being cut from the advance. Its description already says \"Advance auto-applied on invoice generation\".\r\n\r\nStep 6 — Add the download buttons\r\n\r\nPOST /api/app-treasurer/flat-ledger/download-pdf\r\nPOST /api/app-treasurer/flat-ledger/statement/download\r\nRemember to send delivery=link and open the returned link without any header, same as the reports screen.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Balance column never goes below zero. So if a resident is in credit, that column shows 0.00, not 800.','2026-08-21 06:37:33','2026-08-21 06:37:33',NULL,0),(5580,1863,'Issue',13,'totalUnpaidAmount	₹ amount still to collect — matches the web exactly\r\nunpaidInvoices	        count of invoices still owing\r\npartiallyPaidInvoices	count of part-paid invoices','2026-08-21 06:42:37','2026-08-21 06:42:37',NULL,0),(5581,1859,'Issue',13,'1. Add small text under the ₹5,300:\r\n\r\n\r\nOutstanding Dues\r\n₹5,300\r\nas on today\r\nJust those three words fix the whole confusion.\r\n\r\n2. Fix the title. The API already sends this:\r\n\"period\": { \"fromDate\": \"2026-07-01\", \"toDate\": \"2026-07-02\", \"mode\": \"CUSTOM\" }\r\nIf mode is FY → show \"Financial Summary (YTD)\"\r\nIf mode is CUSTOM → show \"Financial Summary (01 Jul – 02 Jul 2026)\"','2026-08-21 06:53:31','2026-08-21 06:53:31',NULL,0),(5582,1857,'Issue',13,'Call GET /api/app-treasurer/gst/settings when the screen opens.\r\nIf GST is off → hide the \"GST Applicable\" checkbox and the GST % dropdown entirely, and show a short note: \"GST is not enabled for this society.\"\r\nIf GST is on → show them as normal.\r\n\r\n','2026-08-21 08:24:00','2026-08-21 08:24:00',NULL,0),(5583,1796,'Issue',13,'','2026-08-21 08:46:25','2026-08-21 08:46:25',NULL,0),(5584,1779,'Issue',13,'Show the server\'s message on failure instead of a fixed \"Failed to send reminder\".','2026-08-21 09:16:49','2026-08-21 09:16:49',NULL,0),(5585,2371,'Issue',13,'<img style=\"width: 2107px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608211502-yprpz.png\"><br>\r\n<img style=\"width: 474px;\" src=\"clipboard-202608211503-yzyuc.png\"><br>\r\n','2026-08-21 09:39:50','2026-08-21 09:39:50',NULL,0),(5586,1883,'Issue',13,'Change one URL per screen to show only necessary accounts in all following screens\r\n\r\nScreen	Use this\r\nCreate Invoice	GET /api/app-treasurer/accounts/for-invoice\r\nBulk Invoice	GET /api/app-treasurer/accounts/for-invoice\r\nCreate Expense	GET /api/app-treasurer/accounts/for-expense\r\nCreate Bill	GET /api/app-treasurer/accounts/for-expense\r\nCredit Note	GET /api/app-treasurer/accounts/for-invoice\r\nChart of Accounts screen	keep GET /api/app-treasurer/accounts — it should show everything\r\n','2026-08-21 10:05:28','2026-08-21 10:05:28',NULL,0),(5587,1884,'Issue',13,'','2026-08-21 10:08:19','2026-08-21 10:08:19',NULL,0),(5588,2090,'Issue',13,'If the flat search still fails then check is what the app sends — it should be:\r\n\r\n\r\nGET /api/visitor/search-flat?search=1&societyId=<selected society>','2026-08-21 10:24:42','2026-08-21 10:24:42',NULL,0),(5589,2040,'Issue',14,'','2026-08-21 11:18:54','2026-08-21 11:18:54',NULL,0),(5590,2211,'Issue',8,'','2026-08-24 04:05:12','2026-08-24 04:05:12',NULL,0),(5591,1807,'Issue',7,'','2026-0