 advances don\'t see an empty block.\r\n\r\nStop computing the counts on the client. That\'s the cause of the \"0 Entries\" you saw — the server now sends count and remainingCount for the whole society, not just the page that happens to be loaded.\r\n\r\nDon\'t compute remaining as total − adjusted. Use the field. It\'s the live balance on open rows, so it always matches the balances in the list; deriving it would drift on a cancelled row.','2026-09-01 12:26:05','2026-09-01 12:26:05',NULL,0),(6169,2385,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-01 12:34:03','2026-09-01 12:34:03',NULL,0),(6170,2371,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-01 12:35:41','2026-09-01 12:35:41',NULL,0),(6171,2372,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-01 12:38:19','2026-09-01 12:38:19',NULL,0),(6172,2226,'Issue',7,'Credit note created but the invoive is not getting downloaded in the app.\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 322px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609011815-qvuvy.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n__________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIn the admin side, attchemnt is not shown in first time, it shows in the second click.\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 1559px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609011816-veazk.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\nAlso in the admin side, invoice is downloaded but amount of credit note is not shown properly and correct. \r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 1559px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609011819-4hw51.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n','2026-09-01 12:52:53','2026-09-01 12:52:53',NULL,0),(6173,2122,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 12:54:41','2026-09-01 12:54:41',NULL,0),(6174,1945,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-01 13:00:59','2026-09-01 13:00:59',NULL,0),(6175,2080,'Issue',7,'<img style=\"width: 302px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609011830-khynp.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nas discussed, current month che paid karayche amount nahi aali ani amount hi highlighted asli pahije.','2026-09-01 13:01:15','2026-09-01 13:01:15',NULL,0),(6176,1952,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 13:08:36','2026-09-01 13:08:36',NULL,0),(6177,1884,'Issue',7,'bulk invoice generate kele, generate zale pn jya flats la residents assign nahi ahet tyanchya card vr kahich mention nahi jase ki resident map nahiye kinva NA, tr tithe kahitri user friendly tag dakhwawa lagel admin ani app madhe.\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 311px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609011849-a6ifv.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n_________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n<img style=\"width: 1578px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609011849-tq1xj.png\"><br>\r\n','2026-09-01 13:19:31','2026-09-01 13:19:31',NULL,0),(6178,1495,'Issue',13,'Get the pre-approved visitor list\r\n\r\nGET /api/visitormanagement/resident/get-preapprove-request?page=1&limit=10\r\nAuthorization: Bearer <guard token>\r\nEach visitor in the response now has 5 new fields:\r\n\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"46bb23dc-...\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Yash\",\r\n  \"scheduledVisitDate\": \"2026-09-01\",\r\n  \"scheduledVisitTime\": \"17:00:00\",\r\n\r\n  \"scheduledAt\":       \"2026-09-01T11:30:00.000Z\",\r\n  \"cancelAvailableAt\": \"2026-09-01T11:30:00.000Z\",\r\n  \"expiresAt\":         \"2026-09-01T18:29:59.000Z\",\r\n  \"canCancel\": false,\r\n  \"isExpired\": false\r\n}\r\nWhat they mean:\r\n\r\nField	Meaning\r\ncanCancel	true = show the Cancel button as enabled. false = keep it disabled.\r\nisExpired	true = the day is over, grey out the row.\r\ncancelAvailableAt	The time the button turns on. Use it for a hint like \"Can be cancelled after 5:00 PM\".\r\nexpiresAt	11:59:59 PM of the visit date.\r\nscheduledAt	The visit time as one full timestamp.\r\nAll three timestamps are UTC (that\'s what the Z means) — convert to local time before showing. 11:30 UTC is 5:00 PM India time.\r\n\r\n2. Cancel the request\r\n\r\nPUT /api/visitormanagement/visitor/{id}/cancel-visitor-request\r\nAuthorization: Bearer <guard token>\r\n\r\n{ \"cancellationRemarks\": \"Visitor did not arrive\" }\r\nRemarks are required, max 500 characters.\r\n\r\n3. What the app should do\r\nDo not calculate the time in the app. Just read canCancel. The backend already worked it out.\r\nButton rule: canCancel: true → enabled. canCancel: false → disabled.\r\nRefresh matters. If the guard opens the screen at 4:55 PM, canCancel is false. It becomes true at 5:00 PM only when the list is fetched again — so refresh on pull-to-refresh, or when the screen comes back into focus.\r\nHandle the error too. If the call is made too early or too late, the server replies 400 with a ready-made message — show it as-is:\r\n\"This visit is scheduled for 01 Sep 2026, 05:00 PM. It can be cancelled only from the scheduled time onwards.\"\r\n\"This pre-approval has expired — it was valid only until 11:59 PM on its scheduled date.\"\r\nExpired rows: show them greyed out with no buttons. They stay in the list; they are just not actionable.\r\nNothing else in the response changed, so existing fields keep working.','2026-09-01 13:19:50','2026-09-01 13:19:50',NULL,0),(6179,1882,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 13:22:47','2026-09-01 13:22:47',NULL,0),(6180,1881,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 13:23:05','2026-09-01 13:23:05',NULL,0),(6181,1879,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 13:23:46','2026-09-01 13:23:46',NULL,0),(6182,1878,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 13:24:09','2026-09-01 13:24:09',NULL,0),(6183,1507,'Issue',9,'','2026-09-01 13:24:35','2026-09-01 13:24:35',NULL,0),(6184,1507,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-01 13:26:13','2026-09-01 13:26:13',NULL,0),(6185,1955,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-01 13:26:28','2026-09-01 13:26:28',NULL,0),(6186,1883,'Issu