→  { \"approvedVisitors\": 3, ... }\r\n point the \"Approved Visitors\" card at approvedVisitors instead of whatever it reads today. Everything else is unchanged.','2026-09-07 12:19:44','2026-09-07 12:19:44',NULL,0),(6328,2437,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:19:59','2026-09-07 12:19:59',NULL,0),(6329,2436,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:20:09','2026-09-07 12:20:09',NULL,0),(6330,2435,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:20:26','2026-09-07 12:20:26',NULL,0),(6331,2433,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:20:56','2026-09-07 12:20:56',NULL,0),(6332,2432,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:21:09','2026-09-07 12:21:09',NULL,0),(6333,2431,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:21:19','2026-09-07 12:21:19',NULL,0),(6334,2402,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:21:42','2026-09-07 12:21:42',NULL,0),(6335,1863,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:22:39','2026-09-07 12:22:39',NULL,0),(6336,1779,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:31:07','2026-09-07 12:31:07',NULL,0),(6337,1495,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:35:55','2026-09-07 12:35:55',NULL,0),(6338,2441,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-07 12:42:23','2026-09-07 12:42:23',NULL,0),(6339,2440,'Issue',13,'1. Add Tenant — allow only one flat (Resident App)\r\n\r\nOn the Add and Edit Tenant screen, the flat list is multi-select. Make it single-select. Tapping a second flat should replace the first, not add to it. Same on Edit Tenant.\r\n\r\nKeep sending flatIds as an array — it just carries one flat id now.\r\n\r\nIf you don\'t change it, the server will reject it and send back this message, which you can show directly to the user:\r\n\r\nSelect one flat for this tenant. To rent out a second flat, add a separate tenant for it.\r\n\r\nReason: one tenant = one flat. Each flat has its own rent agreement, its own visitor requests, and its own bills. If a resident rents out two flats, they add two tenants — even if it\'s the same person.','2026-09-07 12:53:45','2026-09-07 12:53:45',NULL,0),(6340,2399,'Issue',13,'GET /visitormanagement/federation-gate/societies\r\n\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"totalSocieties\": 2,\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"totalSocieties\": 2,\r\n    \"totalVisitorsToday\": 1,\r\n    \"arrivedAtSociety\": 0,\r\n    \"pendingApproval\": 0,\r\n    \"preApprovedCount\": 3,     ← the Pre-approved Visitors card\r\n    \"totalResidents\": 30       ← newly added\r\n  },\r\n  \"societies\": [ …one entry per society, with the same counts… ]\r\n}\r\n\r\nAdd a Pre-approved Visitors card to the Federation Security dashboard, reading summary.preApprovedCount','2026-09-07 13:01:17','2026-09-07 13:01:17',NULL,0),(6341,2409,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-08 04:27:13','2026-09-08 04:27:13',NULL,0),(6342,2386,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-08 04:27:56','2026-09-08 04:27:56',NULL,0),(6343,2388,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-08 04:28:18','2026-09-08 04:28:18',NULL,0),(6344,2226,'Issue',13,'Resident app — receipt not downloading after online payment\r\n\r\nAfter a successful payment, the receipt download fails with \"Could not download invoice\".\r\n\r\nReason: the success screen sends the Razorpay payment id (pay_TZQYVXnUoRsrjR) to the receipt API. The server does not store that id, so it cannot find the payment.\r\n\r\nFix (easy, please do this one):\r\n\r\nThe verify API already returns a transactionId in its response. Use that for the receipt download instead of the Razorpay id.\r\n\r\n\r\nverify response  →  { \"transactionId\": \"92d2aae6-...\", ... }\r\nSend transactionId to the receipt download API. It works today, and it also works for older payments.\r\n\r\nYou can still show pay_TZQYVXnUoRsrjR on screen as \"Transaction ID\" — just don\'t send it to the download API.\r\n\r\nSecond thing, please check:\r\n\r\nWhen you call the verify API, please make sure you are sending all three fields that Razorpay\'s checkout gives you:\r\n\r\n\r\nrazorpay_order_id\r\nrazorpay_payment_id      ← this one may be missing\r\nrazorpay_signature\r\nWe checked the database: for about half the successful payments, razorpay_payment_id is empty. The server saves it only if the app sends it. Please confirm all three are being sent.','2026-09-08 05:42:38','2026-09-08 05:42:38',NULL,0),(6345,2409,'Issue',9,'','2026-09-08 07:27:27','2026-09-08 07:27:27',NULL,0),(6346,2080,'Issue',13,'Treasurer app — Maintenance Billing Setup, \"Generate Now\" button\r\n\r\nWe changed the rules on the server. Please stop deciding the button state in the app and read it from the API.\r\n\r\n1. Use the new fields\r\n\r\nEvery setup returned by the setup list / detail API now includes:\r\n\r\n\r\n\"canGenerateNow\": true,\r\n\"generateBlockedReason\": \"OK\",\r\n\"generateBlockedMessage\": \"\",\r\n\"targetMonth\": 9,\r\n\"targetYear\": 2026,\r\n\"targetPeriodLabel\": \"September 2026\",\r\n\"cycleGenerated\": false,\r\n\"autoWindowPassed\": false,\r\n\"scheduledRunAtLabel\": \"10 Sep 2026, 10:00 AM\"\r\ncanGenerateNow = true → show the button enabled\r\ncanGenerateNow = false → show it disabled, and show generateBlockedMessage as the reason\r\nPlease do not work out the enabled/disabled state from status, auto-generate or dates in the app. The server already does it, and if the app calculates it separately the two will disagree.\r\n\r\n2. Send the period the server gives you\r\n\r\nWhen calling generate, send targetMonth and targetYear from the API response. Don\'t calculate the month in the app.\r\n\r\n\r\nPOST /app-treasurer/maintenance/generate/:id\r\n{ \"month\": <targetMonth>, \"year\": <targetYear> }\r\n3. Handle the error properly\r\n\r\nThe server now blocks generation in these cases and returns 400 with a readable message:\r\n\r\nSetup is not active\r\nInvoices for this month were already generated\r\nAuto Generate is ON and its scheduled time has already passed\r\nPlease show the message from the response directly to the user. Don\'t show a generic \"something went wrong\".\r\n\r\n4. What the button should look like\r\n\r\nSetup	Auto Generate	Before scheduled time	After scheduled time\r\nInactive	ON	disabled	disabled\r\nActive	ON	enabled	disabled\r\nInactive	OFF	disabled	disabled\r\nActive	OFF	enabled	enabled, until generated once\r\nYou don\'t need to code this table — canGenerateNow already gives you the answer. It\'s just so you know what to expect while testing.\r\n\r\nAlso note: activating a setup no longer sends invoices. That was the bug. Invoices go out only at the scheduled time (Auto Generate ON) or when the user presses Generate Now.','2026-09-08 07:30:27','2026-09-08 07:30:27',NULL,0),(6347,2386,'Issue',13,'For BOTH apps (Federation Security + Society Security)\r\nStop deciding the buttons in the app. Read them from the API.\r\n\r\nEvery staff row now comes with this:\r\n\r\n\r\n\"gateState\": \"ARRIVED_AT_FEDERATION\",\r\n\"gateStateLabel\": \"Arrived at federation gate\",\r\n\"isFederationGated\": true,\r\n\r\n\"canRecordArrival\": false,\r\n\"canRecordArrivalBlockedMessage\": \"Arrival already recorded for this visit\",\r\n\r\n\"canCheckIn\": true,\r\n\"canCheckInBlockedMessage\": \"\",\r\n\r\n\"canCheckOut\": false,\r\n\"canCheckOutBlockedMessage\": \"Staff has not checked in yet\"\r\nRules:\r\n\r\ncanX = true → show the button enabled\r\ncanX = false → show it disabled, and show the matching BlockedMessage as the reason\r\nPlease do not work the state out from isInside or hasArrivedAtGate any more. The server decides now. If the app calculates it separately, the two will disagree.\r\n\r\nYou don\'t need to refresh after a tap. Every action API returns the new state in its response — just use it to update the row.\r\n\r\nLive updates: both apps now receive socket events when the other app acts (staff_checkin_recorded, staff_checkout_recorded, and the arrival event). Each carries the same state block, so you can update the row directly.\r\n\r\nisFederationGated: false means this staff member is not part of the two-gate flow (federation\'s own staff, or a society not under a federation). They behave exactly as before — nothing changes for them.\r\n\r\nFor the FEDERATION Security app\r\nButton: Record Arrival → POST /staff/federation-gate-arrived/:id\r\n\r\nWhat changed:\r\n\r\nIt used to return success and quietly do nothing if arrival was already recorded. Now it returns 400 with a message. Please show that message.\r\nAfter the society checks the staff member out, this button becomes enabled again for the next visit. That\'s expected — it\'s a new cycle.\r\nFor the SOCIETY Security app\r\nButtons: Check In → POST /staff/checkin/:id, Check Out → POST /staff/checkout/:id\r\n\r\nWhat changed:\r\n\r\nCheck In now returns 400 if the federation hasn\'t recorded arrival yet:\r\n\"Federation Security has not recorded this staff member\'s arrival at the gate yet\"\r\n\r\nCheck Out returns 400 if the person hasn\'t checked in.\r\nPlease show these messages to the guard instead of a generic error.','2026-09-08 08:36:19','2026-09-08 08:36:19',NULL,0),(6348,2226,'Issue',8,'give proepr clarification and api of this and full bosy also ','2026-09-08 09:05:51','2026-09-08 09:05:51',NULL,0),(6349,2080,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 10:04:03','2026-09-08 10:04:03',NULL,0),(6350,2443,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 10:22:03','2026-09-08 10:22:03',NULL,0),(6351,2442,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 10:35:55','2026-09-08 10:35:55',NULL,0),(6352,2441,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 10:39:09','2026-09-08 10:39:09',NULL,0),(6353,2440,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 10:46:03','2026-09-08 10:46:03',NULL,0),(6354,2439,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 11:34:46','2026-09-08 11:34:46',NULL,0),(6355,2438,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 11:35:15','2026-09-08 11:35:15',NULL,0),(6356,2434,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 11:43:55','2026-09-08 11:43:55',NULL,0),(6357,2430,'Issue',8,'only test no need to key changes','2026-09-08 12:16:33','2026-09-08 12:16:33',NULL,0),(6358,2429,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 12:43:34','2026-09-08 12:43:34',NULL,0),(6359,2428,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 12:44:23','2026-09-08 12:44:23',NULL,0),(6360,2427,'Issue',8,'','2026-09-08 12:49:28','2026-09-08 12:49:28',NULL,0),(6361,2426,'Issue',8,'its webpage so we can not directly apply dark mode on this ','2026-09-08 12:51:29'