r Dashboard → Financial Summary → the green Total Collected card\r\nAPI: GET /api/app-treasurer/dashboard\r\n\r\nThe problem\r\n\r\nThe small \"Invoices\" chip under Total Collected is picking up the wrong value from the API.\r\n\r\nIt is showing totalIncomeInvoiced → ₹68,22,898 (this is the total invoiced amount)\r\nIt should show totalIncome → ₹5,73,956 (this is the amount actually collected)\r\nWhy it is wrong\r\n\r\nThe two small chips are meant to add up to the big number above them:\r\n\r\n\r\nInvoices  +  Opening Balance  =  Total Collected\r\nRight now it shows 68,22,898 + 0 = 5,73,956, which is impossible. It makes it look like the society collected ₹68 lakh when they collected only ₹5.7 lakh.\r\n\r\nChange 1 — use the right field\r\n\r\nIn the Invoices chip, read totalIncome instead of totalIncomeInvoiced. Nothing else changes. Do not touch the big Total Collected number, it is already correct.\r\n\r\nChange 2 — hide the chips when Opening Balance is 0\r\n\r\nIf openingBalanceCollected is 0, don\'t show the two chips at all. When it\'s 0, the Invoices chip is just the same number as the big one above it, so it adds nothing. This is exactly what the web does.\r\n\r\nHow to test — Greenwood Heights\r\n\r\nAfter the fix the card should show:\r\n\r\nTotal Collected: ₹5,73,956\r\nNo chips below it (because Opening Balance is ₹0)\r\nAnd to check the chips still work, use any society that has settled an opening balance — there, Invoices + Opening Balance must add up to Total Collected.','2026-09-10 11:34:12','2026-09-10 11:34:12',NULL,0),(6457,2453,'Issue',7,'<img style=\"width: 1596px;\" src=\"clipboard-202609101710-23oja.png\"><br>\r\n','2026-09-10 11:40:47','2026-09-10 11:40:47',NULL,0),(6458,2452,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-10 11:41:24','2026-09-10 11:41:24',NULL,0),(6459,2451,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-10 11:42:06','2026-09-10 11:42:06',NULL,0),(6460,2449,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-10 11:42:40','2026-09-10 11:42:40',NULL,0),(6461,2437,'Issue',7,'','2026-09-10 11:43:36','202