 \"date\": \"12/09/2026\",\r\n        \"time\": \"3:29:43 PM\",\r\n        \"status\": \"Resolved\",\r\n        \"subject\": \"App Issue\"\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"sender\": \"avigo_admin\",\r\n        \"replyFrom\": \"admin\",\r\n        \"message\": \"fhfgjhfgjh\",\r\n        \"senderLabel\": \"Avigo Admin\",\r\n        \"senderIsTicketRaiser\": false,\r\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-12T10:00:27.000Z\"\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\nWhat the app should do\r\n1. Show senderLabel above every message. It\'s ready to display — no mapping needed:\r\n\r\n\r\nLila Gaikwad (Resident)     ← from data.raisedByLabel (the Issue Description)\r\nAvigo Admin                 ← from reply.senderLabel\r\nSociety Admin\r\n2. Use senderIsTicketRaiser for left/right, not \"is it mine\". That\'s the actual bug — deciding by \"mine\" makes every message look the same to anyone who isn\'t one of the two people talking:\r\n\r\n\r\nsenderIsTicketRaiser === true   → left  (the person who raised it)\r\nsenderIsTicketRaiser === false  → right (whoever is answering)\r\n3. The round avatar letter should come from senderLabel, not from the ticket creator. Right now it uses the creator for every bubble, which is why the same letter appears on both sides.\r\n\r\nNotes\r\nsender and replyFrom are unchanged — nothing existing breaks.\r\nPossible senderLabel values: Avigo Admin, Society Admin, Federation Admin, Resident, Security, Treasurer, Family Member, Tenant, Federation Security — and the raiser gets Name (Role).\r\nTreat them as display text only. For logic, use sender or senderIsTicketRaiser.\r\nAlready live in the response once the backend is deployed — no new endpoint, no app-side mapping table.','2026-09-12 12:47:27','2026-09-12 12:47:27',NULL,0),(6613,2515,'Issue',13,'','2026-09-15 04:22:12','2026-09-15 04:22:12',NULL,0),(6614,2520,'Issue',9,'','2026-09-15 06:40:55','2026-09-15 06:40:55',NULL,0),(6615,2523,'Issue',9,'already working','2026-09-15 06:44:08','2026-09-15 06: